CI writes per-arch slices and a universal fat binary:

- `termx-capture-arm64` / `termx-capture-x86_64` / `termx-capture`
- `termx-virtual-display-arm64` / `termx-virtual-display-x86_64` / `termx-virtual-display`

Termx picks `*-$(uname -m)` when it matches, otherwise the fat file.

Sign locally (Command Line Tools, no Xcode):

```bash
cp helpers/macos/signing/signing.env.example helpers/macos/signing/signing.env
# edit identity / p12
helpers/macos/sign.sh
```
